  "proof_invariants": [
    "Every actual finite stored label has a simple-path witness; nonnegative cycles cannot give a strict improvement.",
    "Scanning an edge in a wave establishes its Bellman inequality relative to the wave-entry source label.",
    "Every successful atomic decrease is notified; every notification target decreased somewhere in that wave, though that atomic may have failed.",
    "Every successful update to a value at most delta is notified into re; re may also contain an above-delta target after classification rereads a decreased source.",
    "At epoch entry all dirty sources are in the initial frontier; at wave boundaries Dirty is contained in frontier union deferred.",
    "Actual epoch transform d_next <= T(d_entry), using the original worklist schedule; after V-1 epochs values are final, then at most one drain epoch.",
    "For clipped low labels D, all dirty low sources are in retry frontier and D_next <= T_delta(D); low values settle within V-1 waves.",
    "Once low values settle, any further re notification would imply a target low decrease or a source low decrease; therefore wave V empties re."
  ],
